01:03:33,333 --> 01:03:39,333
Son of the South is a 2020 American biographical historical drama
film, written and directed by Barry Alexander Brown.

12
01:09:20,000 --> 01:09:26,000
Based on Bob Zellner's 2011 autobiography, The Wrong Side of Murder Creek: A White Southerner in the Freedom Movement, Lucas Till portrays Zellner, with Lex
Scott Davis, Lucy Hale, Jake Abel, Shamier Anderson, Julia Ormond, Cedric the Entertainer and Brian Dennehy appearing in supporting roles.

13
01:15:06,666 --> 01:15:12,666
Spike Lee serves as an executive producer.

14
01:20:53,333 --> 01:20:59,333
It had its world premiere at the American Black
Film Festival on August 26, 2020.

15
01:26:40,000 --> 01:26:46,000
It was released on February 5, 2021, by Clear Horizon Entertainment and Vertical
Entertainment, receiving mixed reviews from critics, however praising Till's performance.

16
01:32:26,666 --> 01:32:32,666
The film explores themes of alabama, civil rights,
based on true story, racism, klansmen.

17
01:38:13,333 --> 01:38:19,333
The tone is emotional.
